Title: Chapter 1: Intelligence Needs Bodies
Creation-Date: 2026-07-03
Last-Modified: 2026-10-04
Output-Formats: 
Tagline: A brain without a body is a brain without an error-correction mechanism. Deterministic computation, sensory grounding, and the shop class that doesn't tolerate fooling around. Then the world model that is a simulation in motion, theory of mind as its most demanding case, and the shield Perseus was given instead of a better eye: you never inspect another mind, you work from a reflection of it. Three jobs for one faculty, and the position that they are one architecture.
